Metadata --> Data processing procedures	Data analysis procedures	Description of the data processing and analysis procedures used to obtain specific test results, e.g. percentage elastic extension, ee			Mandatory	To convert the primary data series into the processed data series a validated excel template (lab own's development) was used. The data were neither averaged nor smoothed. See also file "Vh5205_Complementary_Data-processing.LIS"
Metadata --> Data processing procedures	Workflow usage	Were automated (user-independent) analysis workflows used?			Mandatory	No	
Metadata --> Data processing procedures	Software	If applicable, please list the used software/workflow, including product and version			Mandatory	Not applicable	
Metadata --> Data processing procedures	Related publications	If applicable, please list  publications related to the data analysis procedure/software used			Optional		
Primary data --> Test result --> Values recorded at test start	Minimum test piece diameter at room temperature		D	mm	Mandatory	6	*
Primary data --> Test result --> Values recorded at test start	Original gauge length		Lo	mm	Mandatory	24	*
Primary data --> Test result --> Values recorded at test start	Parallel length		Lc	mm	Mandatory	36	
Primary data --> Test result --> Values recorded at test start	Extensometer gauge length		Le	mm	Mandatory	22.5	*
Primary data --> Test result --> Values recorded at test start	Determination of reference length	Case 1: Reference length for calculation of percentage extensions/elongations if the original gauge length Lo and/or extensometer Le are inside the parallel length, Lc. In this case Lr = Le (percentage extensions) or Lr = Lo (percentage elongations).
Case 2: Reference length for calculation of percentage extensions/elongations if the original gauge length Lo and/or extensometer Le are outside the parallel length, Lc. In this case, Lr, for calculation of percentage is corrected to consider the strain contributions of the shoulders/ridges.
			Mandatory	Case 1	
